st. Working group Limited Additional Mechanisms for PKIX and SMIME ( ...\n\n[3] Media Access Control (MAC) Addresses in X.509 Certificates\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc10031/\nIETF Protocol and Documentation Usage. RFC 9542, LAMPS Working Group mailing list … published August 2026\n\n[4] RFC 10003: Certificate Management over CMS (CMC)\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc10003/\nJuly 2026; Authors: J. Mandel, S. Turner. Working group: Limited Additional Mechanisms for PKIX and SMIME (LAMPS); Area: Security Area (SEC); Publication Stream ...\n\n[5] RFC 9919: The Lightweight Online Certificate Status ...\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9919/\nDate published July 2026. Working group Limited Additional Mechanisms for PKIX and SMIME (LAMPS) Area Security Area (SEC) Publication Stream IETF DOI\n\n[6] Search\nhttps://www.rfc-editor.org/search/\nSearch RFCs by number, title, subseries, author, etc. Working group Search working group. IETF publication Operations and Management Area Show abstract ... …","u":false},{"n":3,"a":"SEARCH('https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc10003/')","r":"From the search results, I can see several LAMPS RFCs published in July or August 2026:\n- RFC 10003: Certificate Management over CMS (CMC) - July 2026\n- RFC 9919: The Lightweight Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) - July 2026\n- RFC 9925: Unsigned X.509 Certificates - February 2026 (not July/August)\n- RFC 10031: Media Access Control (MAC) Addresses in X.509 Certificates - August 2026\n\nI need to find the page counts for these RFCs to determine which is the shortest. Let me check the RFC Editor's records for ea …","s":"Page https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc10003/:\nRFC 10003: Certificate Management over CMS (CMC): Transport Protocols | RFC Editor\nYour browser has JavaScript disabled. Most of this site works without JS, but some features require it. If something seems broken please try enabling JavaScript and reloading the page.\nThe JavaScript used by this site is served di